      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Got some more intel for ya--some of the deforms seem to be (mostly) local. The neck and torso look normal for other players, though the knees are still bent (appearing as in the half-body position). The current \"fix\" that me and a pal (shoutout to KillerKuru) found is rejoining the instance. The issue comes back whenever you recalibrate FBT within VRC, but it can be \"fixed\" by rejoining the instance each time you calibrate. It's kind of annoying, but I suppose it's a decent enough fix temporarily if anyone stumbles across this! \n\nFor reference, I also snapped an image of the err... issues. Again, this happens when the model is under 1 meter tall, getting more extreme the smaller it gets. In terms of my actual rig, it is properly set to be small, and the issue resides only in VRC this patch.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
